Apr 30, 2026

Dear Brother and Sister Killian,

We are grateful to report that on 4 Jun 2026, Elder Kaden Killian will be r=
eturning to your family in Lindon, UT, having faithfully completed his duti=
es as a missionary in the Japan Kobe Mission. His stake president will offi=
cially release him from full-time service shortly after his arrival.

Elder Killian is a wise, thoughtful, kind, caring, compassionate missionary=
 who always works faithfully and cheerfully. He served diligently in leader=
ship positions as Trainer for two assignments and helped new missionaries g=
ain their confidence and grow into fine missionaries. His dedicated service=
 in the Japan Kobe Mission will be remembered warmly in the hearts of many.

Sister Sano and I are deeply grateful for the love and example that Elder K=
illian radiated during his missionary service and for the opportunity to wo=
rk with him here. It is inspiring to witness the joy in Elder Killian's cou=
ntenance as he prepares to be reunited with you, his beloved family. I am d=
eeply grateful to you for allowing your son to serve as a missionary in Jap=
an at this time. May God's choicest blessings be granted upon you and your =
family.

Upon completing the mission, Elder Killian will receive an email from the M=
issionary Department containing a copy of the "Certificate of Missionary Se=
rvice" including the signature of the President of the Church. This email c=
ontains instructions for downloading additional copies from churchofjesusch=
rist.org.

We love your son and thank you for your continued support.

Best regards,

President and Sister Sano

Japan Kobe Mission



--_000_SA0PR04MB7403FF57246128EA140EA1C7E6352SA0PR04MB7403namp_
